{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01351",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 4.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.04,
      "end_seconds": 9.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.4,
      "end_seconds": 19.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Okay, so doctor, it's numbness in my feet. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.08,
      "end_seconds": 23.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Did it it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.03,
      "end_seconds": 28.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Ever since... since Friday, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.94,
      "end_seconds": 43.95,
      "duration_seconds": 14.01,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.46,
      "end_seconds": 70.27,
      "duration_seconds": 24.81,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day. Yes, night. That makes it worse. Oh, you know, and being unsteady in the dark. That's been about the same, two weeks. I've also had burning pain in my toes, for six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.94,
      "end_seconds": 73.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.41,
      "end_seconds": 85.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.27,
      "end_seconds": 117.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "okay: blood pressure 114 over 73, respiratory rate 17. And heart rate 76, saturation 99 percent, temperature is 36.8 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.37,
      "end_seconds": 122.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.05,
      "end_seconds": 124.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.91,
      "end_seconds": 128.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.44,
      "end_seconds": 144.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "The ankle reflexes are reduced and the feeling is dulled below the knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.05,
      "end_seconds": 149.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.03,
      "end_seconds": 164.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Right, and what about back pain, bladder problems or weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.15,
      "end_seconds": 167.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "no, not a single one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.2,
      "end_seconds": 172.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "and your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.29,
      "end_seconds": 177.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.13,
      "end_seconds": 181.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Okay, is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.13,
      "end_seconds": 184.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.05,
      "end_seconds": 195.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.55,
      "end_seconds": 202.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "I mean, I take gliclazide, 80 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.37,
      "end_seconds": 207.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.32,
      "end_seconds": 210.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "no, it's at home"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.46,
      "end_seconds": 213.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.4,
      "end_seconds": 217.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.17,
      "end_seconds": 221.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.82,
      "end_seconds": 226.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.48,
      "end_seconds": 246.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.51,
      "end_seconds": 250.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Mm, I've had diabetes, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.3,
      "end_seconds": 277.58,
      "duration_seconds": 26.28,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, my working impression is a peripheral neuropathy, probably related to diabetes. Another possibility is a low vitamin B12. We should do a nerve conduction study for neuropathy. I'm going to order a B12 level, for neuropathy. The treatment will be amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, long term. It's for nerve pain. Check both feet daily and wear well-fitting shoes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.97,
      "end_seconds": 286.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.81,
      "end_seconds": 291.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "thank you, you know, that's clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.77,
      "end_seconds": 297.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.34,
      "end_seconds": 300.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "I'll remember that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.7,
      "end_seconds": 309.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "We'll catch up in four weeks. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.47,
      "end_seconds": 323.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "so, I take the amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.74,
      "end_seconds": 330.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.58,
      "end_seconds": 334.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "That's clear, um, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.18,
      "end_seconds": 336.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}